WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.560
Welcome back, dear viewers of SCP Explained.

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:07.430
We hope you’ve been keeping well, and we
also hope that your health insurance covers

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:13.640
blown minds, because today, we’re using
our trademark Anom-O-Tron 6000 to pit an anomalous

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:16.219
legend against another Marvel legend.

00:00:16.219 --> 00:00:24.369
That’s right - it’s SCP-682 Vs Dr. Michael
Morbius, of the 2022 cinematic masterpiece,

00:00:24.369 --> 00:00:25.369
Morbius.

00:00:25.369 --> 00:00:30.450
Of course, there is one issue that we should
share with you before we begin: We haven’t

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:31.650
actually seen Morbius.

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:35.870
However, here’s the wonderful thing - Statistically,
you haven’t either.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:41.680
In fact, we tried to get the Anom-O-Tron 6000
to process Morbius as raw data for the simulation,

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.180
but our antivirus software kept stopping it.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:45.180
Intriguing.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:49.660
So instead, we simply hit “Randomize Traits”
on the Anom-O-Tron, so it’s free to use

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:55.280
advanced AI to conceive what Morbius is like,
and what his abilities probably are.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.960
And as far as you or I know, it might even
be correct.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:03.219
So let’s get this show on the road, and
see if the Hard to Destroy Reptile could hold

00:01:03.219 --> 00:01:07.439
its own at cinema’s most tragically memed-upon
superhero.

00:01:07.439 --> 00:01:14.680
Prepare for perhaps the most absurd and ridiculous
video we’ve ever released on here.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:17.610
In other words, it’s Morbin Time.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:24.050
It began, as many bizarre SCP Foundation stories
do, with SCP-682 cracking the glass of its

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:28.650
acid tank and preparing to spill chaos and
terror out into Site 19.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:33.370
For most people, even seeing actual footage
of this would be a life-defining traumatic

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:34.370
incident.

00:01:34.370 --> 00:01:38.000
For most seasoned Foundation researchers,
it was just another Sunday.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:43.500
When 682 busted through the nearest wall like
a psychopathic, reptilian Kool Aid man, while

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:47.860
guards engaged in the futile task of trying
to subdue it with small arms fire, the senior

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:53.040
researchers languidly made their way to the
nearest secure panic room and hunkered down.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:58.649
As was standard protocol for SCP-682 escapes,
all available Mobile Task Force units would

00:01:58.649 --> 00:02:03.530
be dispatched, single-mindedly focused on
cutting the lizard back down to size.

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:09.429
But the problem was, this wasn’t just any
other Sunday, it was Super Bowl Sunday - and

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:13.920
seeing as most Mobile Task Force operatives
are incredibly tough and manly, they generally

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:18.550
love football, and promised they’d definitely
come and take down 682...

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:20.310
As soon as the game was over.

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:25.680
This would be one thing if SCP-682 was content
to just terrorize the usual denizens of Site

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.489
19 today, but no.

00:02:27.489 --> 00:02:32.401
It’d been a while since the Hard to Destroy
Reptile had tasted civilian flesh, and he

00:02:32.401 --> 00:02:35.269
intended to rectify that tout suite.

00:02:35.269 --> 00:02:40.610
In a state of murderous fury, 682 barged through
wall after all with the effort that a normal

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:43.200
human being might walk through rice paper.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:47.269
Soon enough, it was free from the drab gray
walls of the containment site, and feeling

00:02:47.269 --> 00:02:49.880
the sun on its scales once more.

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:54.850
Such a lovely day out, with the distant sound
of people laughing and chatting, and children

00:02:54.850 --> 00:03:00.990
playing happily with their pets. 682, predictably,
found this disgusting, and resolved to destroy

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:01.990
them all.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:06.030
And with all those Mobile Task Force operatives
swigging beer, eating peanuts, and giggling

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:11.040
at amusing celebrity cameos in Super Bowl
half time ads, there would be nobody who would

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.250
stop 682 from completing its dastardly task.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:19.590
Except, of course, one man: Dr. Michael Morbius.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:24.820
While 682 was escaping, Morbius was sitting
on the deck of his private yacht, drinking

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:29.909
a martini glass full of two percent milk - because
Morbius understands the importance of having

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.330
healthy bones.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:36.260
He was listening to a fascinating podcast
about the curative powers of beef jerky when,

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:41.730
high above, the SCP Foundation activated the
Morb Signal: A Batman-esque light shining

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:44.290
up in the sky in the shape of a clown.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.590
This was bad.

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:50.430
Morbius paused his podcast and prepared himself,
finishing the last of his milk and washing

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.819
out the glass so it didn’t get smelly.

00:03:52.819 --> 00:03:58.349
He raised his arm and summoned the Morb Orb
- a glowing red ball that seems to be the

00:03:58.349 --> 00:04:01.950
source of his powers, according to a number
of internet memes.

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:06.500
He clutched the Orb, feeling its power flow
through him, as he made a small prayer to

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:09.330
his guardian deity, the late David Bowie.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:14.239
And with that, he took flight, twin jets of
fire blasting out of his shoes like rocket

00:04:14.239 --> 00:04:15.239
ships.

00:04:15.239 --> 00:04:20.820
He could only hope that he’d be able to
intercept SCP-682 before it was too late.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:25.860
Meanwhile, SCP-682 was indulging in one of
his favorite hobbies: Just killing lots of

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:26.860
people.

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:31.350
He’d invaded the American city of San Fran
Angeles, New York, which is known for being

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:35.000
the biggest population of people within the
proximity of Site 19.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:40.400
682 was truly rampaging - He knocked the ice
cream cones out of children’s hands, causing

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:41.800
them to weep profusely.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:43.729
He literally kicked dogs.

00:04:43.729 --> 00:04:47.759
And he also murdered a number of adults with
his vicious fangs and claws.

00:04:47.759 --> 00:04:51.789
The local police attempted to stop him, but
they were hopelessly outmatched.

00:04:51.789 --> 00:04:55.900
They attempted to cuff the monster several
times, only to find out that by the time they

00:04:55.900 --> 00:05:00.180
were half way through trying to read the beast
its Miranda Rights, it would break free and

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:01.720
rampage yet again.

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:06.669
All in all, SCP-682 was having a grand old
time, and was delighted that nobody was coming

00:05:06.669 --> 00:05:09.600
to stop its rampage of utter devastation.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:14.199
It seemed almost as though the rampage would
never end, until a dark shadow fell over the

00:05:14.199 --> 00:05:15.979
ravenous reptilian monster.

00:05:15.979 --> 00:05:19.480
It turned up its head to see a new foe floating
above it.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:20.650
Was it a bird?

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:21.660
Was it a plane?

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:27.240
No, it was Dr. Michael Morbius, of course,
wielding his trademark flaming trident of

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:28.240
justice.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:31.340
“Another lamb to the slaughter,” 682 growled.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:34.630
“Are you ready to meet your end?”

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:36.000
Morbius laughed and shook his head.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:40.600
“I don’t know what you are, you scaly
monster, but for hurting all these innocent

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:43.449
people, you’re about to get morbed on!”

00:05:43.449 --> 00:05:48.759
And with that, he threw his flaming trident
at the reptile, striking brave and true - But

00:05:48.759 --> 00:05:50.620
it wasn’t enough.

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:55.150
682 had developed incredibly strong reflexes
after years of the Foundation’s attempts

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:59.740
on its life, so Morbius would need to try
a lot harder than just using his classic,

00:05:59.740 --> 00:06:02.410
beloved trident to end this fight.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:06.790
Even then, before Morbius had a chance to
think up another method of attack, 682 had

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:08.930
adapted and switched to the offensive.

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:14.760
Two great, dragon-like leathery wings unfurled
on the monster’s back, and it took air,

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:18.360
lunging towards Morbius with fangs borne and
claws at the ready.

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:22.220
Before Morbius knew it, the creature’s jaws
were ready to close around his head.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:26.620
Thankfully, at this moment, another one of
Morbius’ classic superpowers comes into

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:29.940
play: His short-range teleportation abilities.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:34.810
In a moment of reflex that would impress 682,
Morbius teleported out of the monster’s

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:38.470
path, remanifesting instantly, floating a
few feet away.

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:40.430
682 growled in irritation.

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:44.490
“Of course it would never be so easy,”
it said.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:48.470
“The Foundation always ends one of its freaks
to distract me.

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:53.030
You may think you’re strong, but really,
you’re just another puppet.”

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:56.960
“I’ve never heard of this Foundation,”
Morbius quipped back.

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:59.849
“And I’m not your standard hero, either.

00:06:59.849 --> 00:07:03.620
I really blur the line between Hero and villain
entirely.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:04.780
In fact—“

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:11.699
Before Morbius could finish explaining what
a complex character he was, 682 flew after

00:07:11.699 --> 00:07:12.699
him again.

00:07:12.699 --> 00:07:14.669
This time, however, Morbius was ready.

00:07:14.669 --> 00:07:20.000
He lifted up his arms and unleashed another
one of his patented attacks: Opening up human

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:25.539
mouths in the palm of his hands, which unleash
miniature yet still extremely powerful air

00:07:25.539 --> 00:07:26.730
to air missiles.

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:34.009
The missies blasted out and struck 682, causing
an impressive explosion, but 682 was well-versed

00:07:34.009 --> 00:07:35.009
in explosions.

00:07:35.009 --> 00:07:37.289
It kept flying after Morbius.

00:07:37.289 --> 00:07:41.710
He needed to get out of here, fast, or he’d
become a lizard’s lunch.

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:46.810
Morbius turned and flew in the opposite direction,
the Hard to Destroy Reptile hot on his heels.

00:07:46.810 --> 00:07:50.919
The first step, of course, would be to get
away from populated areas to limit collateral

00:07:50.919 --> 00:07:52.009
damage.

00:07:52.009 --> 00:07:56.979
No matter what happened, Morbius refused to
let this mysterious entity harm more people.

00:07:56.979 --> 00:07:59.409
“You can’t run forever!”

00:07:59.409 --> 00:08:00.620
682 growled.

00:08:00.620 --> 00:08:05.060
“Your wretched life will be brought to a
slow and painful end, stranger!”

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:09.419
They were passing over the water now, flying
at quantum speeds, watching the Pacific Ocean

00:08:09.419 --> 00:08:10.909
whizz past beneath them.

00:08:10.909 --> 00:08:14.759
That’s when Morbius noticed it, and had
an epiphany: A volcano!

00:08:14.759 --> 00:08:19.500
And by the looks of the smoke rising above
it, an active one, too!

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:23.990
Morbius had a plan now, but to execute it,
he’d need perfect speed and timing.

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:29.900
He stopped in mid air as the beast flew towards
him - But moments before 682 could make contact,

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:35.030
Morbius grabbed it, executing a perfect mid-air
suplex, and tossing the roaring beast directly

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:37.330
down into the volcano below.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:40.039
For any other monster, that would be the end
of it.

00:08:40.039 --> 00:08:46.990
But for 682, a double, triple, or even quadruple
tap was often required to reliably incapacitate

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:47.990
it.

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:49.290
Morbius’ work was not done.

00:08:49.290 --> 00:08:54.250
He flew down towards the volcano, ready to
engage in the next hectic stage of battle.

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:58.920
“Bet you’re not feeling so cocky now,
you nasty reptile!”

00:08:58.920 --> 00:08:59.959
Morbius yelled.

00:08:59.959 --> 00:09:04.920
But the reptile in question was too busy flailing
around in impossibly hot magma to reply at

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:09.300
the time, such is the way when falling into
an active volcano.

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:15.350
SCP-682, burnt and charred, but alive, began
to crawl from the top of the volcano, wheezing

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:16.589
out smoke and ash.

00:09:16.589 --> 00:09:20.910
How could such a strange, confusing creature
have been such a formidable opponent?

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:27.230
No matter, it will destroy this “Morbius”,
it might just take a little longer than expected.

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:32.089
Little did the unfortunate reptile know, Morbius
was preparing his next weapon, perfect for

00:09:32.089 --> 00:09:37.870
immobilizing this ornery monster: An 8-ball
in a gym sock, forming a kind of dangerous

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:39.230
makeshift flail.

00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:43.450
It was the kind of lethal improvised weapon
that would strike fear into even one of the

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:44.820
strongest enemy combatants.

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:50.220
And now, SCP-682 would learn to fear its power.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:54.760
As the flame-broiled reptile began to stand,
perhaps preparing to adapt to its latest set

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:59.870
of injuries, Morbius began relentlessly beating
the Hard to Destroy Reptile with the 8-ball

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:05.390
sock, dazing it with repeated brutal strikes
that seemed to never stop.

00:10:05.390 --> 00:10:09.600
Morbius had learned this technique from years
of being involved in vicious bar fights, normally

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:12.020
caused by him cheating at darts.

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:16.060
“This can stop any time you want,” Morbius
yelled.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:19.550
“You just need to stop getting back up.”

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:24.370
Initially, 682 wanted to remain defiant, but
even it couldn’t deny that being struck

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:28.970
again and again by the 8-ball sock was actually
extremely painful.

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:30.860
Was it really worth the fight?

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:37.889
After performing some quick mental calculations,
SCP-682 determined that no, it probably wasn’t.

00:10:37.889 --> 00:10:39.579
Time to throw in the towel.

00:10:39.579 --> 00:10:44.680
“Okay, Okay,” 682 said, mostly annoyed
at this point.

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:45.779
“I’ll stop rampaging.

00:10:45.779 --> 00:10:49.100
Honestly, you just took all the fun out of
it.”

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:54.320
682 just sighed and laid on the ground, exhausted,
slowly regenerating from its injuries.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:57.139
Morbius smiled, content with his victory.

00:10:57.139 --> 00:11:01.680
Who knows how many people he’d saved by
luring this creature away from a population

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:02.680
center?

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:06.680
By this point, the Super Bowl was over, and
the legions of Mobile Task Force operatives,

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:11.430
who technically should have done this hours
ago, finally decided to suit up and take care

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:12.430
of business.

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:17.050
It didn’t take long for black tactical helicopters
full of Foundation soldiers managed to triangulate

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:22.660
the location of the volcano where the end
of 682 and Morbius’ epic battle had taken

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:23.660
place.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:27.110
It wasn’t long after that that there were
copious Foundation boots on the ground.

00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:30.200
The story, of course, has a happy ending:

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:35.950
Mobile Task Force Agents successfully recaptured
SCP-682 and returned it to the containment

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:37.980
cell in Site 19.

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:42.700
And in the process of recovery, they mistook
Dr. Michael Morbius for the actor Jared Leto,

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:47.500
and shot him roughly 30 times in the chest
with armor-piercing rounds, killing him instantly.

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:48.839
Want an anomaly of your own?

00:11:48.839 --> 00:11:53.200
Check out www.scpswag.com for high-quality
SCP merch!

00:11:53.200 --> 00:12:00.540
Now go and check out “SCP-096 Vs Siren Head”
and “SCP-076 ABLE VS CHAINSAW MAN...

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:02.209
WHO HAS THE MOST LETHAL WEAPON?”

00:12:02.209 --> 00:12:03.140
for more wild Vs battles!

